[TITLE]
AquaOptima dPHM-PINN Sprint 15 — small reference EPANET .inp fixture
with a throttle-control valve (TCV). Three-node topology:

    R1 (suction reservoir, fixed head 50 m)
      |
      +-- V1 (TCV, K = 2.5, 150 mm) --> J1 (elev 0, no consumer)
                                          |
                                          +-- P1 (pipe, 200 m, 150 mm)
                                                |
                                                +-> J2 (15 L/s consumer)

The dPHM importer routes the TCV row through the conservative
resistance surrogate ``fit_tcv_resistance_surrogate``. The surrogate
chooses an effective Hazen-Williams length that reproduces the
minor-loss head loss ``K * V^2 / (2 g)`` at the network's total
positive demand (15 L/s). The translation is bounded, finite, and
Newton-stable, but it matches the minor-loss term only at the anchor
flow — off-design flows diverge because |Q|^1.852 vs K*Q^2 disagree.
See docs/epanet-inp-import.md for the exact assumptions and
limitations.

SI flow units (LPS), Hazen-Williams head loss. Solvable by
aquaoptima.dphm.newton_solve with jacobian_mode="analytic".

[JUNCTIONS]
;ID   Elev   Demand   Pattern
 J1   0.0     0.0     ;     ; TCV discharge node (no consumer)
 J2   0.0    15.0     ;     ; 15 L/s consumer

[RESERVOIRS]
;ID   Head   Pattern
 R1   50.0   ;          ; 50 m fixed-head suction reservoir

[PIPES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Length   Diameter   Roughness   MinorLoss   Status
 P1   J1      J2      200.0    150.0      130.0       0.0         OPEN

[VALVES]
;ID   Node1   Node2   Diameter   Type   Setting   MinorLoss
 V1   R1      J1      150        TCV    2.5       0

[OPTIONS]
 Units                LPS
 Headloss             H-W

[END]
